# CP10 — the discrimination failure. Last modelling checkpoint.
#
# Diagnosed before fixing (G1-G4), then one change at a time. The answer was
# G2: post-hoc isotonic calibration was erasing the resolution of the quantity
# the policy ranks on, and the criterion the model is selected by could not see
# it. A92 makes the calibrator a selection candidate and adds a resolution
# floor; A93 fixes a feature that should have varied across candidates and did
# not.

SPEC.md
